{:frontmatter
 {:id "adr-2607110300-kotoba-lang-net-kotobase-cloud-murakumo-decentralization-roadmap"
  :title "ADR-2607110300: kotoba-lang / net-kotobase / cloud-murakumo -- 「分散型経済/ブロックチェーン」を名乗るための統合ロードマップ"
  :status "accepted"
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "distributed-economy-blockchain-roadmap"
  :authoritative true
  :last_verified "2026-07-11"
  :authoritative_for
  ["design-only roadmap connecting kotoba-lang (identity/ledger/witness-quorum), net-kotobase
    (storage backend), and cloud-murakumo (economic settlement) into one trust chain --
    no code changes in this ADR, implementation is follow-up work per phase"
   "reuses ADR-2607030030's existing Phase 1/2/3 vocabulary and gates rather than inventing a
    new phase scheme; does not overturn 'no new L1' / 'proof-of-compute is the Phase 3 gate' /
    cljc-only (no Rust extension, ADR-2607071900) decisions already accepted"
   "the concrete new architectural move: wire kotoba-lang/witness-quorum's existing N-of-M
    threshold-signature logic onto kotoba-lang/murakumo's existing overlay QUIC transport
    (murakumo/src/murakumo/overlay/) instead of building a new transport -- this also happens
    to satisfy ADR-2607030030 Phase 2's own stated gate ('overlay の QUIC/WebRTC 結線')"
   "kekkai's existing governor.cljc (Governor abstraction, same shape as the CLAUDE.md Actor
    pattern) is the extension point for turning kekkai from network-reachability governance
    into value governance (treasury release allow/deny driven by witness-quorum slashing
    verdicts), rather than building a new governance component"
   "the label '分散型経済/ブロックチェーン' is explicitly gated to a new Phase 4 (independent
    third-party witness operators with real economic stake) that this ADR only sketches the
    shape of and does not design in detail or implement -- Phases 1-3 completing does NOT
    license using that label externally"]
