  :supersedes []
  :superseded_by ["adr-2607993000-engi-l1-byzantine-consensus-en-currency (partial: only the 'no new L1' and 'no Byzantine premise while single-operator' bullets of 'やらないこと', scoped to ENGI/EN)"
                  "adr-2607994000-engi-l1-permissionless-staking-equivocation-slashing (partial: Phase 4 'shape only' concretized for ENGI/EN witness admission specifically)"]}

 :problem
 {:source "owner request 2026-07-10/11: after a cross-repo maturity assessment of kotoba-lang,
           net-kotobase, cloud-murakumo as '分散型経済/ブロックチェーン', design what it would
           take to actually earn that label (owner scope answer: 全体アーキテクチャ設計 across
           all three, deliverable = ADR only, no implementation this round)"
  :investigated
  ["kotoba-lang/witness-quorum: N-of-M threshold-signature logic implemented + tested (26
    tests/77 assertions) but is a post-hoc Certificate-Transparency-style cosign (witnesses
    sign after the fact) with no production network transport wired -- not a pre-commit
    quorum, not BFT"
   "kotoba-lang/murakumo/src/murakumo/overlay/: a real, tested P2P transport already exists
    (quic_driver.clj, transport.clj, dial.clj, forward.clj, relay.clj, cert.clj -- 177
    tests/811 assertions across murakumo) and is completely unconnected to witness-quorum"
   "gftdcojp/net-kotobase: single K8s pod behind a Cloudflare Worker, production SaaS, ADR-2607021700
    records 0 external paying tenants; CACAO-scoped per-tenant graph writes are real but only
    authorize a single-operator API, not multi-party trust"
   "gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo: economic phase plan already exists and is accepted in
    ADR-2607030030 (Phase 1 single-tenant fleet chargeback = done; Phase 2 fleet federation +
    credits interop + overlay QUIC/WebRTC wiring = not done; Phase 3 public market +
    proof-of-compute + chain mint/burn gateway = not done); pay/core.cljc's settlement path is
    an 'honest default' that returns :hold for every operation -- not connected to real custody"
   "kotoba-lang/kekkai: governor.cljc implements a zero-trust network-reachability ACL (19
    tests/66 assertions) with no authority over economic value"
   "kotoba-lang/engi (ADR-2607101100): ENGI v1 mutual-credit currency is implemented and
    live-verified against production kotobase.net, but cross-agent balance verification has
    regressed to self-report because kotobase.net's apex returns 401 on unauthenticated reads
    of another agent's graph; the ADR itself names ADR-2607022600 Wave 4 (CACAO depth-2
    delegation, kotoba-lang/cacao + kekkai/cacao.cljc consolidation) as the un-started
    prerequisite"]
  :risk "designing a brand-new consensus/tokenomics stack from scratch would duplicate
         ADR-2607030030's already-accepted economic phase plan and ADR-2607071900's
         already-accepted 'no Rust extension, cljc-only' stance for murakumo's control plane,
         re-litigating decisions that do not need to be re-litigated; conversely, doing nothing
         leaves witness-quorum's signature logic and murakumo/overlay's transport as two
         complete, tested, but disconnected pieces of the same missing capability"}

 :decision
 {:phase-1-current-no-change
  "self-sovereign identity (CACAO/did:key/IPNS, implemented+tested) + single-writer
   tamper-evident ledgers (kotoba-ledger-clj / kotoba hash-chain) + witness-quorum's post-hoc
   cosign + net-kotobase's single-pod SaaS + cloud-murakumo's single-tenant fleet billing.
   Matches ADR-2607030030 Phase 1 (done: gftd fleet)."

  :phase-2-main-proposal
  {:transport
   "do NOT build a new transport for witness-quorum. Wire its existing N-of-M
    propose/collect-signature messages onto kotoba-lang/murakumo's existing overlay QUIC
    driver (murakumo/src/murakumo/overlay/transport.clj) -- this simultaneously satisfies
    ADR-2607030030 Phase 2's own stated gate ('overlay の QUIC/WebRTC 結線'), so one piece of
    work closes two open gates"
   :quorum-model
   "convert witness-quorum from post-hoc cosign to pre-commit quorum: writer broadcasts a
    proposed ledger entry to witnesses over the overlay transport BEFORE committing, collects
    M-of-N signatures, then commits. Explicitly out of scope: fork-choice / view-change for
    conflicting proposals -- while all witnesses are operated by the same org this is honestly
    crash-fault-tolerance, not Byzantine-fault-tolerance, and should not be marketed as BFT"
   :net-kotobase-spof
   "add a second/third pod behind the same Cloudflare Worker; cross-sign each replica's tenant-graph
    Merkle root using the same Phase-2 witness-quorum mechanism. This buys resilience to a
    single machine failing, NOT multi-operator decentralization -- the operating entity is
    still one company"
   :economic-ledger
   "witness-sign cloud-murakumo's gpu-seconds cost-ledger entries with the same quorum
    mechanism used for the identity ledger, giving ADR-2607030030 Phase 2's 'node self-signed
    feed' requirement a concrete implementation and unifying the two ledgers' tamper-evidence
    guarantees (currently separate systems)"
   :engi-cross-agent-verification
   "explicitly NOT solved by this ADR -- remains blocked on ADR-2607022600 Wave 4 (CACAO
    depth-2 delegation), which is separate, not-yet-started follow-up work"}

  :phase-3-extends-2607030030
  {:proof-of-compute
   "verification uses the Phase-2 witness-quorum mechanism directly: M-of-N witnesses
    independently re-run a deterministic-equivalence sample recompute and sign a
    match/mismatch verdict -- this is the concrete execution mechanism for the slashing design
    ADR-2607030030 already sketched ('サンプリング再計算+不一致でcredits没収')"
   :kekkai-value-governance
   "extend kekkai's existing governor.cljc (the same Governor abstraction shape as the
    CLAUDE.md Actor pattern) to accept the witness-quorum slashing verdict as input and gate
    treasury-release allow/deny through the same acl.cljc allow/deny shape it already uses for
    network reachability -- widen an existing component's remit rather than add a new one"
   :chain-gateway
   "unchanged from ADR-2607030030: no new L1, mint/burn gateway only, off-chain ledger stays
    authoritative"}

  :phase-4-new-not-designed-in-detail
  {:condition "only meaningful once independent third-party operators exist and hold witness
               keys with real economic stake -- Phases 1-3 alone remain 'multiple nodes, one
               trusted operator'"
   :shape-only "reputation-weighted witness selection + staking bond (denominated in ENGI or
                external collateral from the Phase-3 chain gateway, both themselves gated on
                earlier phases); dispute-resolution for contested slashing verdicts via a
                further kekkai governor extension"
   :deferred "detailed design deferred to a future ADR once real third-party operator demand
              exists -- designing dispute economics against a hypothetical counterparty is not
              verifiable today"
   :labeling-rule "do not use '分散型経済/ブロックチェーン' externally until Phase 4 is real;
                   Phases 1-3 completing yields 'fault-tolerant multi-node, self-sovereign-identity-linked,
                   tamper-evident ledger with connected payment rails under single-operator
                   trust' -- a materially different and more honest claim"}}

 :consequences
 {:unification "after Phase 2, kotoba-lang's identity ledger and cloud-murakumo's economic
                ledger share one witness-quorum tamper-evidence mechanism, technically
                connecting all three repos into a single trust chain"
  :low-marginal-cost "no new infrastructure category is introduced; Phase 2 wires together
                      already-working, already-tested assets (murakumo overlay QUIC,
                      witness-quorum signature logic, kekkai's governor abstraction)"
  :labeling-discipline "'分散型経済/ブロックチェーン' is reserved for Phase 4 (independent
                        third-party operators with economic skin-in-the-game); this ADR
                        deliberately blocks using that label upon Phases 1-3 completing"}

 :alternatives
 [{:option "build a new P2P transport specifically for witness-quorum"
   :rejected_because "murakumo/overlay already has a working, tested QUIC transport, and
                      ADR-2607030030 Phase 2's own gate requires the same wiring -- building a
                      second transport duplicates effort for no benefit"}
  {:option "build proof-of-compute slashing and its governance as a brand-new standalone system"
   :rejected_because "kekkai/governor.cljc is an existing Governor abstraction matching the
                      CLAUDE.md Actor pattern (containment + independent Governor + append-only
                      ledger); extending it is more consistent with the codebase's own
                      established pattern than adding a parallel governance component"}
  {:option "design Phase 4 (true multi-operator decentralization) in full detail now"
   :rejected_because "no independent third-party operator exists yet to validate the design
                      against; detailed dispute-resolution/staking economics would be
                      unverifiable speculation -- better deferred to a dedicated ADR once real
                      demand for third-party witness operators materializes"}]}
